      "general": {
        "abstract": "The Fuji Hokuroku Flux Observation Site (FHK) (35° 26'N, 138° 45'E, 1100m above sea level) is located in a mature larch forest of 55-60 years old at the foothills of Mt. Fuji. The micrometeorological, meteorological and biomass measurements were started in 2006. Active studies are now conducted for technological development of various gas flux measurement methods, including other greenhouse gases such as methane. \r\nThe site is also used for ground measurement to validate satellite remote sensing data, various training programs, and joint investigations with Asian researchers.",
